{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And the sheep Jacob separated.</b> And he did yet another thing: he separated the sheep and chose from them every speckled one and every dark one, and set the face of the flock toward them, until they would bear thus, and so they became his flocks alone, and he did not set them upon Laban's flock. And some say that \"and he set himself flocks\" is later, for the sheep he separated from his own flocks:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:27.846698102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}